WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.550
Speaker 1: Let's start with some very important
actually good news today, at least sort of

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:05.910
if the problem gets fixed.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:11.849
A judge has ruled that Ron Desantis's new
redistricting map in the state of Florida

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:14.750
is completely unconstitutional.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:15.750
Not okay.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.110
The lines are going to have to be redrawn.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:21.690
And this is very good news because what was
done in Florida was such a brazen attempt

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.949
to gerrymander to the benefit of Republicans.

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:27.850
And everybody tries to do it whenever they
get the opportunity, they try to do it, there's

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.070
no doubt.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.619
But this was so obvious and so brazen that
we were.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:36.910
If this wasn't stopped by a judge, then all
bets are off.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.730
So we have a very good report from Axios.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:44.660
Florida judge says the Santos redistrict redistricting
map unconstitutional.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:49.550
A Florida judge on Wednesday struck down a
portion of a redistricting map drawn by Florida

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.820
Governor Ron DeSantis and his staff.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.250
A Leon County Circuit judge, Lane Smith, said.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:01.880
I am finding that the enacted map is unconstitutional
under the Fair District Amendment because

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:07.389
it diminishes African-Americans ability to
elect the representatives of their choice.

00:01:07.389 --> 00:01:12.149
A formal order is expected today or tomorrow
to ensure the maps aren't used in November.

00:01:12.149 --> 00:01:18.009
This is a key part, which is not only was
this map found to be unconstitutional, it

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:22.369
can't be allowed to be used in November while
a new map is figured out.

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:25.229
That's an absolutely critical element to this.

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:31.759
DeSantis plan dismantles the north Florida
seat now held by a black Democrat.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:37.829
The new maps DeSantis called race neutral
make it harder for North Florida voters to

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:42.529
elect a black member of Congress in the fifth
Congressional District, where nearly half

00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:43.539
its residents are black.

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:48.930
So the technique that's used here is if you
have, for example, in this case, a district

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:54.450
where you have a black Democrat and nearly
half the residents are black, and you say,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:02:00.119
well, this is this is a seat that, as currently
drawn, is likely to be won again by this elected

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.119
official.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:05.950
What you do is you split that district up
and you put some of the black folks in one

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:10.840
Republican district and some of the black
folks in another, so that in neither district

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.370
do they have a critical mass.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.300
And in this way, you can take one or two seats.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:21.439
And in fact, when we look at the map, the
whole point of the map as drawn is to create

00:02:21.439 --> 00:02:27.849
a whole bunch a whole bunch of easy Republican
districts while making it very difficult for

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:28.849
Democrats to win.

00:02:28.849 --> 00:02:33.049
And of course, if you're looking at this map,
you will see that in southeastern Florida,

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:38.650
the Miami, etc. area, you have a number of
of blue districts.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.739
But these are maps that make it very difficult
for Democrats to win anywhere else.

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:48.159
And part of the way that this is done is by
using general demographic trends.

00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:53.099
Black folks tend to vote more for Democrats
than Republicans in Florida.

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:56.640
And you can you can use that to your advantage.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.159
A Democratic aligned redistricting group joined
voting rights and civil rights organizations

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:07.099
to file suit against this map the same day
it was signed into law late last month.

00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:12.900
And fortunately, because this doesn't always
happen, it was adjudicated or evaluated relatively

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.510
quickly by the judge.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.220
So, listen, nobody's surprised, right?

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:23.170
I mean, this is this is not only the expected
outcome of Ron DeSantis deciding he was going

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.090
to redistrict and draw the maps himself.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:29.730
This is this is a feature, not a bug of what
they do here.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:34.209
And the most important things here are, number
one, that the judge ruled on this quickly.

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:37.379
But number two, that the judge is expected
today or tomorrow.

00:03:37.379 --> 00:03:42.019
Maybe by the time you see this clip, it will
already have been done, not allow these maps

00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:43.959
to be used in November.

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:51.299
And one of the other aspects of this is there
is a sort of I don't want to necessarily call

00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:57.180
it virtue signaling, but it's a sort of virtue
signaling where many things that Ron DeSantis

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.459
has done have not been designed to stand up
to legal scrutiny.

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:05.950
In fact, they were probably done knowing they
wouldn't stand up to legal scrutiny.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:12.290
The point here is to attempt a whole bunch
of stuff to then be able to use it either

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.489
in his reelection campaign, which is getting
going now.

00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:20.840
DeSantis is up for reelection in November
as governor of Florida, or it's theorized,

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.620
and the polling suggests that he may have
a shot.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:29.120
It's theorized that Ron DeSantis may try to
run for president, starting with Republican

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.810
nominee in 2024.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:37.270
And so, you know, opening Florida early to
large sporting events when everything else

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:41.810
was shut down, as we were trying to figure
out in 2020, what is COVID, how does it work,

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:42.810
how contagious is it?

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:48.800
All of these things he can use that the don't
say gay bill, the event to commemorate the

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.539
victims of communism, I think it was called,
which we talked about earlier this week, obviously

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:56.009
unconstitutional congressional maps.

00:04:56.009 --> 00:04:58.510
A lot of this stuff isn't designed to stand
up.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.150
The legal scrutiny because it's not going
to.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:06.389
But it is designed to allow Ron DeSantis to
take credit for it at some point later.

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:07.750
And it wouldn't be.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:13.389
I would be shocked if he didn't do it either
for his gubernatorial reelection campaign

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:17.110
or if he does decide to run for president
in in 2024.

